│  1 What does this part of the code do?                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • This code defines the class CrewAgentExecutor which manages the │
│    execution of an agent’s tasks with tools.                       │
│  • It holds references to the agent, crew, language models, tools, │
│    tool handlers, and an i18n instance.                            │
│  • The key method _use_tool creates a ToolUsage instance which     │
│    handles tool invocation, parsing and error handling based on    │
│    AgentAction input.                                              │
│  • It currently creates ToolUsage with the tools_handler, tools,   │
│    original_tools, tool description strings, function_calling_llm, │
│    task, agent, and action parameters.                             │
│  • Throughout the class, _i18n (an I18N instance) is used for      │
│    error messages and localization.                                │
│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • The bug is due to ToolUsage initializing its own I18N instance  │
│    by default, neglecting the agent’s i18n instance which respects │
│    the crew’s prompt_file and localization.                        │
│  • Here, CrewAgentExecutor creates ToolUsage instances but does    │
│    not pass the agent’s i18n to ToolUsage.                         │
│  • Therefore, ToolUsage cannot produce localized error messages    │
│    reflecting the crew’s customized prompt_file.                   │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • When instantiating ToolUsage inside _use_tool,                  │
│    CrewAgentExecutor should pass the agent's i18n instance to      │
│    ToolUsage.                                                      │
│  • Then ToolUsage would use this shared i18n instead of creating a │
│    new default instance, ensuring message localization             │
│    consistency.                                                    │
│  • The ToolUsage class’s __init__ must be modified to accept an    │
│    i18n parameter and set self._i18n accordingly.                  │
│                                                                    │
│ Summary:                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • The bug fix requires modifying ToolUsage.init to accept an i18n │
│    parameter.                                                      │
│  • The CrewAgentExecutor._use_tool method must be changed to pass  │
│    its agent's i18n when instantiating ToolUsage.                  │
│                                                                    │
